      "id": "multiple-persistent-riders-on-one-attack",
      "status": "unsupported",
      "blocker": "AttackCapabilityDefinition fails closed on purpose: 'Current runtime supports one persistent control rider per attack.' IRON_PIT_RULES_CONTRACT: 'Unsupported outcome-changing mechanics fail closed.' No printed 2014 catalog attack that a fight currently needs carries two persistent control riders; extra on-hit damage plus one grapple or one save rider already compiles."
    },
    {
      "id": "complete-condition-semantics",
      "status": "partial",
      "blocker": "IRON_PIT_RULES_CONTRACT: 'Unsupported outcome-changing mechanics fail closed. Never approximate, silently ignore, or invent a combat-relevant mechanic merely to make a card runnable.' Conditions that are bound (Prone, Blinded, Grappled, Poisoned, and others) resolve through the shared condition identity. Arbitrary remaining printed conditions and every cross-condition interaction stay fail-closed until each is certified."
    },
    {
      "id": "forced-movement-push-pull-teleport",
      "status": "partial",
      "blocker": "IRON_PIT_RULES_CONTRACT: 'Opportunity Attacks, forced movement, Disengage consequences, speed changes, Grappled/Prone movement effects, Frightened movement restrictions, and other combat-relevant movement rules remain RAW where applicable.' Printed save/attack push already resolves. Teleport stays banned: pit limits are no teleport, no plane shift, no summoning, and no vertical flight. A generic pull/teleport compiler is not required to invent those missing printings."
    },
